        "id": 1523269
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-06T14:48:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the link which you have shared - https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/c374893e0cef15cb3689026a719526e248ef03f3/board/redrix/thermal.c#86\n\nisn\u0027t these curve parameters different than the change which is part of this CL? As per my understanding, cureve params are those that decide the fan rpm directly. But as part of temps command we just calculate amount of cooling the sensor might require based on the sensor temperature. This is nothing to do with fan_duty or fan_rpm ? Please do help me with my understand.",
      "parentUuid": "ef6d53b9_78a90aa8",
      "revId": "6190c95efb14bf9636c7c598e70fff3765c3e499",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
